(2848424, 395284, 27847, '<td valign="top">Yes, I agree with the statement above. This shot has great potential but I find it distracting due to the fact the foreground flowers are out of focus and they created a distraction due that that fact. If that was reversed and the background was out of focus it could have great possibilities. My opinion, keep shooting.........</td>', 'Yes, I agree with the statement above. This shot has great potential but I find it distracting due to the fact the foreground flowers are out of focus and they created a distraction due that that fact. If that was reversed and the background was out of focus it could have great possibilities. My opinion, keep shooting.........', '2006-09-19 19:41:49.000000', NULL, 1),
(2848433, 393866, 27847, '<td valign="top">Well what''s the problem, start blowing something up... haha this is chemistry after all! Nice composition and I like the over all lighting around the subject but the shot just doesn''t due much for me overall, maybe not in this chemistry context. But I love the the glasses, hope you didn''t take them from Bubbles - Trailer Park Boys ... hahah<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-09-20 00:12:46.</i></td>', 'Well what''s the problem, start blowing something up... haha this is chemistry after all! Nice composition and I like the over all lighting around the subject but the shot just doesn''t due much for me overall, maybe not in this chemistry context. But I love the the glasses, hope you didn''t take them from Bubbles - Trailer Park Boys ... hahah', '2006-09-19 19:45:48.000000', '2006-09-20 01:12:46.000000', 1),
(2848436, 395313, 27847, '<td valign="top">Good concept, bad border!!! With borders like this one you actually take away from you photo subject and you draw the audience towards the border, never let the border speak for your photography. ;-) Just something I''ve learned</td>', 'Good concept, bad border!!! With borders like this one you actually take away from you photo subject and you draw the audience towards the border, never let the border speak for your photography. ;-) Just something I''ve learned', '2006-09-19 19:47:16.000000', NULL, 1),
