(2849456, 395392, 52449, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Army of nOne:</b></div><hr/><i> Very over chlorinated and acidic enough to wash your skin away.  Food coloring I presume.</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Yes, I used food coloring in order to provide much more contrast than a regular Chlorine or pH test would. Believe it or not, each side of my pool tester only had one drop of food coloring put in. That''s the closest I could come to some sort of pink shade for the Cl. The same happened with the yellow (pH) side.<br/></td>', 'Originally posted by Army of nOne: Very over chlorinated and acidic enough to wash your skin away.  Food coloring I presume.  Yes, I used food coloring in order to provide much more contrast than a regular Chlorine or pH test would. Believe it or not, each side of my pool tester only had one drop of food coloring put in. That''s the closest I could come to some sort of pink shade for the Cl. The same happened with the yellow (pH) side.', '2006-09-20 01:35:27.000000', NULL, 0),
